ers/ace24713","html_url":"https://github.com/ace24713","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-31T12:24:15Z","updated_at":"2026-07-31T12:24:15Z","body":"Mayhaps I should open a separate issue for it, but I was just looking at the code here and I noticed set_custom_viewport doesn't correctly disconnect/connect the \"child_order_changed\" signal.\r\n\r\nLike if you look at the ENTER_TREE and EXIT_TREE code that's the only place those signals are connected and disconnected, and it uses the vp variable to construct the callable. set_custom_viewport changes the vp variable, so that would obviously break, because it'd be connected to the wrong viewport and the disconnect call would fail because the passed in callable has a different target.\r\n\r\nI don't know what that stuff actually does, but to my eye that seems like an obvious mistake.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5142823535/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]